# L §5.11 guards: "in an if ... (if k == 1 then … else …)".  A guard that doesn't suffice is checked per key
# (RUN-KEY): here x[k - 2] at k = 2 lies outside ks = 1..3.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ks = 1..3
input step: int

def x[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = if k == 1 then step else x[k - 1] + step
def y[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = if k == 1 then step else y[k - 1 - 1] + step

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  step = 1

ask q1: x[k] for k in ks law 2026-06-30
ask q2: y[2] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1 (k = 1): 1
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q1 (k = 2): 2
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q1 (k = 3): 3
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q2: refused: RUN-KEY ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
